{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "f76d3c9e-fd1f-45d3-b65a-f5e2681acc9a",
    "name": "Smart Employee & Project Management System",
    "description": "Postman collection for the Smart Employee & Project Management System REST API (Spring Boot backend). Endpoints, request bodies, and enum values here are taken directly from the @RestController classes under backend/src/main/java/com/smartemp/controller/ (AuthController, EmployeeController, ProjectController, TaskController, DashboardController, ReportController) and their DTOs (com.smartemp.dto.request/response, com.smartemp.model.enums). Import this collection, run Login first (it stores the JWT in the `token` collection variable), then exercise the other folders.\n\nNOTE: the backend currently has an unresolved inconsistency between these controllers and some of their services (TaskService/DashboardService/ReportService reference a different, newer entity model) - see the \"Known Backend Inconsistencies\" section in the root README. This collection documents the controller-defined contract as-is; a couple of endpoints (e.g. GET /api/auth/me) are included because they were requested for this submission but are not yet implemented in AuthController.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      { "key": "token", "value": "{{token}}", "type": "string" }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8080", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "token", "value": "", "type": "string" },
